# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NO PROVIDER API KEY BELONGS IN THIS FILE.
#
# The frontend never holds a provider key. It calls the LiteLLM gateway with
# a per-user *virtual* key, minted server-side by api/register-user.js and
# capped by budget. Provider keys (DeepSeek, Gemini, OpenAI) live only in
# litellm-proxy/.env, which is gitignored and never deployed to Vercel.
#
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the browser bundle at build time.
# A real key in a VITE_ variable is published to every visitor, permanently,
# in a file anyone can read. There is no such variable any more — do not add
# one back.
#
# Server-side only (set in the Vercel dashboard, never in this file):
#   LITELLM_MASTER_KEY   — mints per-user virtual keys. Admin credential.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.
# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below is OPTIONAL. Leave it all unset and the app runs in
# preview mode: Calendar, Gmail and digest email use realistic sample data,
# every screen is fully interactive, and each one wears a "Preview" label so
# a demo can't be mistaken for a live connection.
#
# Step-by-step instructions for going live: MANUAL_SETUP.md at the repo root.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Which LiteLLM gateway to call. Not a secret — it is a URL.
# VITE_GATEWAY_URL="https://your-litellm-instance.up.railway.app"

# Per-tier model override. Also not secrets: these are LiteLLM *alias* names,
# resolved to real providers in litellm-proxy/config.yaml. Set these only to
# change a model without editing src/lib/aiConfig.ts.
#   defaults: fast=gemini-2.5-flash-lite  reasoning=deepseek-v4-flash  draft=deepseek-v4-pro
# VITE_AI_MODEL_FAST="gemini-2.5-flash-lite"
# VITE_AI_MODEL_REASONING="deepseek-v4-flash"
# VITE_AI_MODEL_DRAFT="deepseek-v4-pro"

# Local Firebase emulator (auth :9099, firestore :8085). Development only.
# VITE_USE_FIREBASE_EMULATOR=true

# Google Calendar + Gmail. BOTH of these are required for live mode — the
# flag alone, or the client id alone, still falls back to preview, so a
# half-finished .env degrades to a working demo instead of a broken OAuth
# redirect loop.
# VITE_INTEGRATIONS_MODE=live
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="xxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com"

# Base path of the Cloud Function that mediates token exchange and all
# Google API calls. The browser never holds a refresh token.
# VITE_INTEGRATIONS_API_BASE="/api/integrations"

# Transactional email for the dormant-contact digest. The in-app digest
# works without this; only emailing it out needs a provider.
# VITE_EMAIL_MODE=live
# VITE_EMAIL_FROM="you@yourdomain.com"
